From: iOSPlus10 laurel <laurel@local>
Subject: [PATCH] laurel 2850: Metal plug-in names on IOAcceleratorES after a self-check (Adreno 610)

topaz 0138 publishes an empty IOAcceleratorES, so Metal.framework finds no device. Now a thread holds the
service back until the check is done: root mounted (<= 60 s), RedwoodGPU published (<= 20 s after the root),
GPU ready, CHIP_ID 0x0601xxxx (Adreno 610, Turnip FD610), GMEM, NegroniMetal.bundle files in the root. Then it
sets MetalPluginName = NegroniMetal, MetalPluginClassName = NegroniMTLDevice and registers the service; on any
failure it registers it empty, as 0138 did. CoreAnimation polls for IOAcceleratorES (300 x 100 ms), so even
backboardd sees the names. One line: "LAUREL METAL: on: Turnip a610 (...)" or "LAUREL METAL: off: <reason>".
Kill switch: laurelmetal=0 (topaz 0138 behaviour). Design: docs/laurel_sprout/metal.md.

